package hartland

model lexicon locale cs

// The distribution-center dimension's words, Czech. LR ruling 7 (2026-10-11): the demo's 4.1 and 6.1
// («Tržby z tržiště podle distribučního centra v roce 2025») went to the LLM at ~14 s because
// «distribučního centra» bound nothing (G1). The citation form is already a term — the entity's
// `displayLabel.cs` ("Distribuční centrum") — but it is EXACT, and the resolver looks a mention up
// by its dictionary form only when the mention is ONE word (`LemmaLookup`): a Czech multi-word
// term's citation form is not the token-wise lemma of what was written, so a phrase is matched as
// written and the estate declares the forms it means. Hence the case forms below, singular and
// plural, minus the citation form the label already gives.
//
// «sklad» is one word, so its cases («skladu», «skladech») reach it through the lemma lookup.
// One target, `er.entity.warehouse`, the only distribution center in the model.
//
// Watch in rehearsal: «na skladě» ("in stock") is a stock phrase that now mentions the warehouse.

def term warehouse_cs {
    description: "distribuční centrum (its case forms), sklad — the distribution-center dimension"
    for: er.entity.warehouse
    forms: [
        "distribučního centra", "distribučnímu centru", "distribučním centru", "distribučním centrem",
        "distribuční centra", "distribučních center", "distribučním centrům", "distribučních centrech",
        "distribučními centry",
        "sklad"
    ]
}
